<<tag character:Narrator>>
<<tag lore_id:lore_milo_child_drawing>>
Narrator: A drawing is tacked to the timber wall of Milo's lean-to with a single rusted nail.
Narrator: Three figures, rendered in coal and beet-juice red. A woman in a long coat. A girl wreathed in pale lines, glowing.
Narrator: A great round sun looms behind them, divided into thirteen wedges like an apple cut for sharing.
Narrator: At the bottom, in a child's careful hand: "Anastasia. Lirael. The sun comes back."
Narrator: The corner of the page is dog-eared from years of being touched in passing.
===
